#!/bin/sh
# Build the vis fork and install it under a prefix, default ~/.local:
# the binary in PREFIX/bin, the Lua runtime in PREFIX/share/vis, man
# pages in PREFIX/share/man. Re-running rebuilds and reinstalls.
#
# usage: bin/install [PREFIX]
#
# Needs a C compiler, make, Lua 5.x and ncursesw headers, and LPeg for
# that Lua at run time. On Fedora:
#   sudo dnf install gcc make lua-devel ncurses-devel lua-lpeg
# SELinux, TRE and ACL support are enabled when their headers are found.
# User config stays in ~/.config/vis, searched before PREFIX/share/vis.
set -eu
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
PREFIX=${1:-$HOME/.local}
for tool in cc make; do
	command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "bin/install: missing $tool" >&2; exit 1; }
done
./configure --prefix="$PREFIX"
make
make install
printf 'installed: '
"$PREFIX/bin/vis" -v
# LPeg is loaded at run time; without it vis starts but nothing is
# highlighted. Probe through the Lua interpreter when one is present.
if command -v lua >/dev/null 2>&1 && ! lua -e 'require "lpeg"' >/dev/null 2>&1; then
	echo "bin/install: lpeg not found for $(lua -v 2>&1 | cut -d' ' -f1-2); install lua-lpeg" >&2
fi
